  <div class="fc-delta-reason">DA ruling accepted. Mojtaba Khamenei did not deliver an authenticated live speech at Ali Khamenei's state funeral proceedings (July 3-7) — the highest-protocol emergence occasion in 141 days of silence. Communications remain in the established pattern: written text attributed to the Supreme Leader's Office, read by state TV presenters over a still photograph. Ali Khamenei 40-day memorial (chehelom, approximately August 17-18) is the sole remaining protocol occasion within the September 15 horizon. Probability reduced from 0.30 to 0.20 on the weight of the funeral non-appearance.</div>
  <dl class="fc-meta-row">
    <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Mojtaba Khamenei appears in authenticated live video or audio broadcast by IRNA or PressTV within 24 hours of recording, with visible on-screen timestamp or 'LIVE' chyron, independently confirmed by at least 2 TIER1 sources as live-recorded in real time. Reading of written statements by presenters over a still photograph or official seal = NO. Pre-recorded material released without live broadcast markers = NO.</dd>
    <dt>Sources</dt><dd>IRNA, PressTV as primary broadcast sources; Reuters, AP, AFP, BBC, Al Jazeera for TIER1 confirmation of live-broadcast status.</dd>
    <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Masked physical appearance without authenticated audio = NO. Written statements from the Supreme Leader's Office = NO. Unverified social media clips not confirmed by TIER1 = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Pre-recorded video released without live broadcast markers (on-screen timestamp, 'LIVE' chyron) = NO. Speech delivered after EOD September 15 UTC = NO.</dd>
  </dl>
  <div class="fc-indicators">
    <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRNA or PressTV announces live address with on-screen 'LIVE' chyron or broadcast timestamp</span>
<span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Mojtaba authenticated attendance at Ali Khamenei chehelom ceremony (approximately August 17-18)</span>
<span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRGC command statement names Mojtaba in active operational authority context</span>
