  <!-- ========== 5. INSIDE IRAN (descriptive, ~200 words) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · 200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      
<p>IRNA and PressTV ran no live footage of Mojtaba Khamenei in the 48 hours to July 27. His communications continue in the established pattern since March 8: written text attributed to the Supreme Leader&#8217;s office, published on khamenei.ir and the official Telegram channel, then read aloud by state television presenters while a still photograph or official seal occupies the screen. No authenticated audio or video of Mojtaba Khamenei has appeared in the 141 days since his designation. → supports <span class="cite">F10</span> without move</p>

<p>State media framing of the strike pause differed sharply from the US diplomatic frame. IRNA and PressTV did not use language about &#8220;giving talks space&#8221; or characterize the pause as a diplomatic concession. Instead, coverage attributed the halt in US strikes to the effectiveness of Iranian resistance and the costs inflicted on US-affiliated assets. The Iranian military spokesperson&#8217;s public statement, carried verbatim on state media, described Tehran&#8217;s suspension of operations as a controlled, reversible tactical choice tied to reciprocity &#8212; not to negotiations. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

<p>Coverage of Ali Khamenei&#8217;s funeral ceremonies (July 3&#8211;7) used the framing of &#8220;martyrdom&#8221; in the context of &#8220;enemy aggression,&#8221; without specifying mechanism. Mojtaba&#8217;s absence from televised funeral proceedings was not addressed by IRNA or PressTV. The 40-day memorial (chehelom) for Ali Khamenei falls approximately August 17&#8211;18, creating the next protocol occasion at which Mojtaba&#8217;s public presence would be customary and potentially expected by the clergy establishment. No IRGC command statement directly named Mojtaba in an active operational authority context during the July 26&#8211;27 window. → supports <span class="cite">F10</span> without move</p>

    </div>
  </div>

